Subject: [PATCH] feat: draw inline texture and atlas icons in text

FontStrings and GameTooltip lines dropped |T...|t and |A...|a escapes
with the other markup, so text after an icon moved left, measured
widths left the icons out and a line of icons alone measured no height;
the client draws the icons in the line and measures them.

- sim_render::inline_markup splits text into text pieces and icons
  (path or file ID, sizes, offsets, texel rectangle and vertex color of
  |T; atlas, sizes, offsets and color of |A, with or without the colon
  after |A) and sizes them as measured on WoW Forever 1.60.1: a |T
  height of 0 is one line high, a |T without a height takes no room, an
  |A without a width is a square one line high.
- Text with an icon is laid out piece by piece: icons become textured
  quads, atlases draw their own @crop: region, a line is as high as its
  tallest icon with text and icons centered on it, word wrap may move an
  icon to the next line. Text without icons takes the unchanged paths.
- WowFontSystem::measure_markup_width and measure_markup_height back
  GetStringWidth, GetStringHeight, FontString auto width and the
  GameTooltip width and line heights.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
